      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ibn Mahboub, from Abdullah Bin Yahya Al Kahily, from Minhal Al Qassab who said, ",
          "‘I said to him<sup>asws</sup>, ‘What is the limit of the receipt of trade outside the city?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘A <span class=\"iTxt\">Rawha</span> (four <span class=\"iTxt\">Fasakhs</span> – about six miles)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ibn Mahbub has narrated from ‘Abd Allah ibn Yahya al-Kahily from Minhal al-Qassab who has said the following: “I once asked him (the Imam), ‘Alayhi al-Salam, ‘What is the limit of going out to meet a caravan of suppliers?’ He (the Imam) replied, ‘It is a distance of one Rawhah (four Farasikh which is equal to six miles)”’ "
        ]
      }
